===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[strong]], [[rough]] [[fabric]] made up of a [[mixture]] of [[silk]], and [[mohair]] or [[wool]].
#* {{RQ:Donne Poems|collection=Satyres|poem=Satyre IIII|pages=339–340|pageref=339|passage=Are not your Frenchmen neate? Fine, as you ſee, / I have but one frenchman, looke, hee followes mee. / Certes they are neatly cloth'd. I, of this minde am, / Your only wearing is your '''Grogaram'''; / Not ſo Sir, I have more.}}
#* {{RQ:Chapman Eastward Hoe|act=I|scene=ii|url=https://archive.org/details/eastwardhoeasitw00chap/page/n12/mode/1up|passage=I like ſome humors of the Cittie Dames well: to eate Cherries onely at an Angell a pound, good; to dye rich Scarlet black, pretty: to line a '''Grogaram''' gowne cleane thorough with veluet, tollerable; their pure linnen, their ſmocks of 3. li. a ſmock are to be borne withall. But your minſing nicetyes, taffata pipkins, durance petticotes & ſilver bodkins—Gods my life, as I ſhall be a Lady, I cannot indure it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Yamakawa Kikue|authorlink=Yamakawa Kikue|chapter=Dress|translator=‎Kate Wildman Nakai|title=Women of the Mito Domain: Recollections of Samurai Family Life|location=Stanford, Calif.|publisher={{w|Stanford University Press}}|year=2001|page=46|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=SfbyFVdlwPgC&pg=PA46|isbn=978-0-8047-3149-2|passage=They had known nothing of woolen cloth, but now the popularity of obi made of imported '''grogram''' spread like wildfire. This popularity produced various stories in its wake.}}

